  "worked_solution": "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=\u27e8-1,1,1\u27e9$ and $w=\u27e80,2,2\u27e9$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =\u27e80,2,-2\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=\u27e80,2,-2\u27e9.$",
